{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1556641183,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODAxODEyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3361#issuecomment-488018126"},"message":"I like the mimeencoding=binary idea and have implemented it in\ngit-annex.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1556645636,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODA0Mzc4NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3361#issuecomment-488043785"},"message":"Awesome, thank you @joeyh","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1556731431,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4ODM0OTE5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3361#issuecomment-488349192"},"message":"With git-annex-standalone=7.20190322+git133-g59922f1f4-1~ndall+1 in `debian-devel` of neurodebian `mimeencoding` is indeed available and seems to work for this use case:\n\nfirst replicating prior erroneous behavior:\n```shell\n$\u003e datalad create --text-no-annex /tmp/testds1\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/testds1 \ncreate(ok): /tmp/testds1 (dataset)\n\n$\u003e cd /tmp/testds1\n\n$\u003e f=file.json; echo '{\"a\": 1}' \u003e| $f; datalad add $f; ls -ld $f \nadd(ok): /tmp/testds1/file.json (file)\nsave(ok): /tmp/testds1 (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 yoh yoh 118 May  1 13:11 file.json -\u003e .git/annex/objects/w5/f7/MD5E-s9--a01637863c1f9585c3e38cde6ce20940.json/MD5E-s9--a01637863c1f9585c3e38cde6ce20940.json\n```\nadjusting to use mimeencoding\n```shell\n$\u003e echo -e '\\n* annex.largefiles=(mimeencoding=binary)' \u003e\u003e .gitattributes; datalad save -m \"Use mimeencoding\"\nsave(ok): /tmp/testds1 (dataset)\n\n$\u003e f=file2.json; echo '{\"a\": 1}' \u003e| $f; datalad add $f; ls -ld $f                                             \nadd(ok): /tmp/testds1/file2.json (file) [non-large file; adding content to git repository]\nsave(ok): /tmp/testds1 (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n-rw------- 1 yoh yoh 9 May  1 13:12 file2.json\n```\n\nso it works!\n\nbut there is a gotcha, that previous versions of annex would puke if encounter `mimeencoding`:\n```shell\n$\u003e f=file2.json; echo '{\"a\": 1}' \u003e| $f; datalad add $f; ls -ld $f                                             \nCommandError: command '['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'annex', 'add', '--json', '--', '/tmp/testds1/file2.json']' failed with exitcode 1\nFailed to run ['git', '-c', 'receive.autogc=0', '-c', 'gc.auto=0', 'annex', 'add', '--json', '--', '/tmp/testds1/file2.json'] under '/tmp/testds1'. Exit code=1.\ngit-annex: bad annex.largefiles configuration: Parse failure: near \"mimeencoding=binary\"\ngit-annex: add: 1 failed\n-rw------- 1 yoh yoh 9 May  1 13:08 file2.json\n```\nso we would need to boost git-annex version dependency!\n\nFTR - empty zero sized files are added to annex as before and as expected (I think we might reconsider and make those added to git):\n```shell\n$\u003e f=file3.json; touch  $f; datalad add $f; ls -ld $f             \nadd(ok): /tmp/testds1/file3.json (file)\nsave(ok): /tmp/testds1 (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 yoh yoh 118 May  1 13:13 file3.json -\u003e .git/annex/objects/fm/24/MD5E-s0--d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e.json/MD5E-s0--d41d8cd98f00b204e9800998ecf8427e.json\n\n$\u003e file -L --mime file3.json \nfile3.json: inode/x-empty; charset=binary\n```\nif we are to reconsider, that is the rule to use\n```shell\n* annex.largefiles=((mimeencoding=binary)and(largerthan=0b))\n```\nNB file with a single empty line (of size 1) would still be considered binary","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1576872767,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2ODA3MjY5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3361#issuecomment-568072693"},"message":"eh, we should have handled this in #3667.  Now elderly me was whining again\nhttps://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/be_robust_to_additions_of_more_specific_mime_types_to_libmagic___40__e.g._application__47__json__41__/?updated#comment-04459bc7f99ebd74419f145e024e6830\nbefore found this... Not sure what @joeyh would decide on this new issue, so I will submit a PR toward use of mimeencoding","files":null}]}